/F1 10.5 Tf 70 760 Td (? **admin.py:** Registers models for the Django admin site.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 745 Td (? **migrations:** Stores database schema change history.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 730 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 715 Td (4. What is the MVT Model?) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 693 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 678 Td (Django follows the MVT architectural pattern, which stands for **Model-View-) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 663 Td (Template**. MVT is Django's variation of the common MVC pattern. It separates) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 648 Td (an application into layers so that data handling, business logic, and) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 633 Td (presentation can be developed and maintained independently.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 618 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 603 Td (5. Model in MVT) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 581 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 566 Td (The **Model** layer represents the data structure of the application. A model) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 551 Td (is a Python class that usually maps to a database table. Each model field maps) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 536 Td (to a database column.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 521 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 506 Td (Responsibilities of the Model layer include:) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 491 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 476 Td (? Defining database tables and fields.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 461 Td (? Representing relationships between tables.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 446 Td (? Validating data rules at the model level.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 431 Td (? Providing database operations through Django's ORM.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 416 Td (? Supporting migrations when the schema changes.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 401 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 386 Td (Example concept:) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 371 Td () Tj
/F3 9 Tf 62 356 Td (    class Student\(models.Model\):) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 62 344 Td (        name = models.CharField\(max_length=100\)) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 62 332 Td (        email = models.EmailField\(unique=True\)) Tj
/F3 9 Tf 62 320 Td (        created_at = models.DateTimeField\(auto_now_add=True\)) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 308 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 293 Td (In this example, `Student` represents a database table, and `name`, `email`,) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 278 Td (and `created_at` represent columns.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 263 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 248 Td (6. View in MVT) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 226 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 211 Td (The **View** layer contains the logic that handles web requests and returns) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 196 Td (web responses. A view receives an HTTP request, performs required processing,) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 181 Td (interacts with models when needed, and returns a response such as an HTML) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 166 Td (page, JSON data, redirect, or error message.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 151 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 136 Td (Responsibilities of the View layer include:) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 121 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 106 Td (? Receiving and processing user requests.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 91 Td (? Fetching or updating data through models.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 76 Td (? Applying business logic.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 285 30 Td (Page 2) Tj
ET
endstream
