BT
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 760 Td (When a user visits `/students/`, Django calls the `student_list` view.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 745 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 730 Td (9. Request-Response Flow in Django MVT) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 708 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 693 Td (1. A user enters a URL in the browser.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 678 Td (2. Django receives the HTTP request.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 663 Td (3. The URL dispatcher matches the URL to a view.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 648 Td (4. The view executes business logic and may interact with models.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 633 Td (5. The model communicates with the database using the ORM.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 618 Td (6. The view passes data to a template.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 603 Td (7. The template renders the final HTML.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 588 Td (8. Django returns the HTTP response to the browser.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 573 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 558 Td (10. MVT Compared with MVC) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 536 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 521 Td (? In MVC, the **Controller** handles user input and coordinates between Model) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 506 Td (  and View.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 491 Td (? In Django MVT, much of the controller responsibility is handled by Django) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 476 Td (  itself through URL routing and framework internals.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 461 Td (? Django's **View** is closer to the controller in MVC because it contains) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 446 Td (  request-handling logic.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 431 Td (? Django's **Template** is closer to the view in MVC because it controls) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 416 Td (  presentation.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 401 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 386 Td (11. Advantages of the MVT Pattern) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 364 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 349 Td (? **Separation of concerns:** Data, logic, and presentation are organized into) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 334 Td (  separate layers.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 319 Td (? **Maintainability:** Code is easier to update, test, and debug.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 304 Td (? **Reusability:** Apps, models, views, and templates can often be reused.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 289 Td (? **Team collaboration:** Backend developers can work on models and views) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 274 Td (  while frontend developers work on templates.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 259 Td (? **Cleaner code:** Business logic is kept away from HTML presentation.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 244 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 229 Td (12. Important Django Commands) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 207 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 192 Td (? `django-admin startproject projectname` creates a new Django project.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 177 Td (? `python manage.py startapp appname` creates a new app.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 162 Td (? `python manage.py runserver` starts the development server.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 147 Td (? `python manage.py makemigrations` creates migration files from model) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 132 Td (  changes.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 117 Td (? `python manage.py migrate` applies migrations to the database.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 102 Td (? `python manage.py createsuperuser` creates an admin user.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 87 Td (? `python manage.py test` runs tests.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 72 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 285 30 Td (Page 4) Tj
ET
endstream
