/F2 14 Tf 54 760 Td (13. Best Practices) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 738 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 723 Td (? Keep views focused and avoid placing too much logic in templates.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 708 Td (? Use models for data rules and database relationships.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 693 Td (? Use forms or serializers for input validation.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 678 Td (? Split large projects into small reusable apps.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 663 Td (? Store sensitive settings such as secret keys and database passwords in) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 648 Td (  environment variables.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 633 Td (? Write tests for models, views, forms, and important user flows.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 70 618 Td (? Use Django's built-in security features instead of disabling them.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 603 Td () Tj
/F2 14 Tf 54 588 Td (14. Quick Summary) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 566 Td () Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 551 Td (Django is a powerful Python framework for building web applications quickly) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 536 Td (and securely. Its MVT architecture divides the application into Models for) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 521 Td (data, Views for request handling and business logic, and Templates for) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 506 Td (presentation. This structure helps developers create organized, reusable, and) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf 54 491 Td (maintainable web applications.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 285 30 Td (Page 5) Tj
ET
